					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Ex-Hegemony</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Kirishu</b> on <b>June 02, 2005, 05:00:17 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">OMG, I just now saw this topic. <br /><br />Ahh, I miss all of you&nbsp; :missyou:<br /><br />Lol Serepi, what is funny is that I ended up playing the BST as my main again anyways, so only kinda not really&nbsp; :approve:<br /><br />As for me I moved onto EiE, and have loved everyday of it. Great bunch of people in the aliance&nbsp; :bondage:<br /><br />So how is retirment coming along and or the &quot;other&quot; games?</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Ex-Hegemony</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Roinin</b> on <b>June 08, 2005, 05:56:42 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I, sirs, have ascended to WoW, which to this day, has in my opinion, floundered as a MMORPG. Blizzard has no fucking clue how to itemize casters, vesrus melee items in end game, and thus you see a tremdous mudflation to melee vs caster dps in end game. EQ did pretty well towards the end, but as OoW neared end game, you could define melee dps mudflation rather easily.&nbsp; Example given is Rogue doig twice, yes twice the dps (400-450 dps with&nbsp; gutgore/core hound tooth?!?!) as opposed to mage or even warlock hovering at 150-200ish dps in Molten Core/Onyxia.&nbsp; I expect no less as complete bullshit program design in Blackwing Lair, but alas where do i go from here? I await Vangaurd, the most promising game on the horizon, atm.<br /><br />Anyways, not to bitch about&nbsp; itemization, but I have returned to EQ for the time being, and alot of familiar faces have since left. If you wish to chat for whatever, shoot me a tell in the late evenings when I log on (11 cst and onward)&nbsp; or PM me here when ever&nbsp; decide to check this&nbsp; board. I&#039;ve talked to a few Ex- Hegemony people, yet the feeling I&#039;m left with is a hollowness that cannot be described. People who know me may relate to what I had invested, as well as everyone involved in Hege, but shrug, I miss ya&#039;s<br /><br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Ex-Hegemony</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Breaenna</b> on <b>July 05, 2005, 01:38:14 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">lol, i checked out FoT, they folded..&nbsp; Checked out Conviction, told em to kiss my ass...&nbsp; Checked out DA, their ranger hated me cuz i was too seXah.&nbsp; Went to DN and found my play time cut short.&nbsp; So now Im guildless and not playing much till RL calms down..<br /><br />BTW, I tried WoW and loved it for about ummmmm.......6 hours...&nbsp; Then I came back to EQ...</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Ex-Hegemony</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Kelce</b> on <b>July 11, 2005, 02:29:00 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Blizzard has indeed screwed the pooch and as Rionin said, &quot;has no fucking clue how to itemize casters, vesrus melee items in end game&quot;. I hope 1.7 fixes that.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Ex-Hegemony</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Gamehenge</b> on <b>August 02, 2005, 07:11:02 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">hey guys!  gamehenge here :)  /cough <br />well I occasionally play Counter Strike, but that is it, EQ was the only video game i ever got into (axamagoura you punk!).  I have thought of returning to EQ, then I have to quiet that thought like its an old heroin habit.  I do miss you guys alot!&nbsp; We had a tight group going for awhile, and those were some great times while we were underdogs.&nbsp; I miss most of you and I would love to hear from you!!&nbsp; my email is gamehenge420L@yahoo.com please drop me a line and let me know what you all up to now.<br /><br />/smile <br /><br /> </div>
					<br />
